.TH MYGOFRAME 1 "2026-11-10" "MyGOFrame 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mygoframe \- view and record capture-card video and audio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mygoframe
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B MyGOFrame
is a native graphical viewer for V4L2 capture devices.
It provides video format, resolution, frame rate, and color range selection.
PipeWire audio inputs can be monitored through the default or a selected output.
Audio monitoring is disabled until an input is selected.
.PP
The preview preserves the captured video's aspect ratio.
A separate capture window provides video-only content for application sharing.
Press F11 to toggle fullscreen and Escape to leave fullscreen.
.SH RECORDING AND PRESETS
Recording controls select a compatible GPU, H.264, HEVC, or AV1 codec,
bitrate, rate control, and MKV or MP4 output.
Recording starts only when requested and does not replace the live preview.
The capture-card audio input can be recorded while speaker monitoring is off
or muted. Monitoring volume does not change recorded audio gain.
.PP
Named presets save video, audio, and recording settings.
Select a saved preset in the command area to start video without opening settings.
Applying a preset does not start recording.
The app information dialog includes developer details and full component licenses.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-help
Display command-line help.
.TP
.B \-capture-window
Open a separate video-only window when the graphical interface starts.
.TP
.BI \-window-width " pixels"
Set the initial window content width in logical pixels.
The default is 1280 and the minimum is 320.
.TP
.BI \-window-height " pixels"
Set the initial window content height in logical pixels.
The default is 800 and the minimum is 240.
.TP
.B \-list
Print V4L2 devices and PipeWire input and output nodes as JSON.
.TP
.BI \-probe " device"
Print supported video modes for a V4L2 device as JSON.
.TP
.BI \-smoke-video " device"
Capture video without opening a window and report stream status as JSON.
.TP
.BI \-smoke-audio " source"
Monitor a PipeWire source without opening a window and report stream status.
Use a source node identifier returned by
.BR \-list .
Monitoring is silent unless
.B \-volume
is set above zero.
.TP
.BI \-output " node"
Select a PipeWire output for an audio check.
An empty value selects the system default.
.TP
.BI \-format " fourcc"
Select a four-character V4L2 pixel format for a video check.
The default is NV12.
.TP
.BI \-width " pixels"
Set the video check width.
The default is 640.
.TP
.BI \-height " pixels"
Set the video check height.
The default is 480.
.TP
.BI \-fps " rate"
Set the video check frame rate as a decimal or fraction, such as 60000/1001.
The default is 60.
.TP
.BI \-video-backend " backend"
Select auto, cpu, or dma video capture.
The default is auto. DMA capture retains CPU fallback on unsupported GPU paths.
.TP
.BI \-color-range " range"
Interpret input samples as auto, limited, or full range.
The default is auto.
.TP
.B \-measure-latency
Measure capture-to-GPU-texture readiness using native completion fences.
This does not measure physical display or controller-to-display latency.
.TP
.BI \-seconds " duration"
Set the duration of a video or audio check in seconds.
The default is 2 and the maximum is 3600.
.TP
.BI \-volume " percent"
Set audio check volume from 0 to 100.
The default is 0.
.TP
.BI \-smoke-ui-video " device"
Display a capture device in the graphical interface.
Requires a positive
.BR \-smoke-ui-seconds .
.TP
.B \-smoke-ui-pattern
Display a synthetic border and colored corners instead of opening a capture device.
Requires a positive
.BR \-smoke-ui-seconds .
The
.B \-width
and
.B \-height
options select the pattern dimensions.
.TP
.BI \-smoke-ui-seconds " duration"
Close the graphical interface after the specified number of seconds.
The default is 0, which leaves it open.
.TP
.BI \-smoke-capture-window-cycles " count"
Close and reopen the capture window during a timed graphical check.
Requires
.B \-capture-window
and enough
.B \-smoke-ui-seconds
for at least one second per cycle plus one.
The maximum is 16.
.SH EXAMPLES
List available devices:
.PP
.nf
.RS
mygoframe --list
.RE
.fi
.PP
Inspect a video device:
.PP
.nf
.RS
mygoframe --probe /dev/video0
.RE
.fi
.PP
Open the graphical interface with a separate sharing window:
.PP
.nf
.RS
mygoframe --capture-window
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mygoframe/presets.json
Named capture and recording presets. If XDG_CONFIG_HOME is not an absolute
path, the configuration directory defaults to $HOME/.config.
.TP
.I $HOME/Videos/MyGOFrame/
Default recording output directory when no output path is selected.
.SH NOTES
Video capture uses the V4L2 single-planar streaming interface.
Supported formats are YUYV, UYVY, NV12, P010, BGR24, RGB24, and MJPEG.
HDR output and tone mapping are not implemented.
Video and audio checks temporarily open the selected devices.
.PP
PipeWire graph latency and capture-card buffering depend on the active hardware
and session configuration.
Reported frame counters do not measure input-to-display or input-to-speaker latency.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
indicates success.
A nonzero status indicates an argument, device, capture, or graphical startup error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pipewire (1),
.BR v4l2-ctl (1)

